<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34483" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pendīgo</span></b> , inis, f.
		id., lit. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an internal tumor</i>, <i>abscess</i>
			(post-class.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Veg. Vet. 2,
			44</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pendiginem circumcides ad vivum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 55</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a hollow space</i>
			inside of a statue: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">simulacri pendigines,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 6, 201</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
